From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: the taskbar is above the windows, behind a full-screen one

The taskbar was among the windows unless it hid itself: a window dragged over
it covered it (QA VM, Notepad; David: "making an app full screen can draw
over the taskbar" -- which it should, and only then). Windows keeps its
taskbar on top and puts it behind a full-screen window in the foreground.
Now the bar is topmost; a window brought forward or shown (not a menu or a
tooltip, topmost themselves), or the foreground window moving, sends it back
on top -- through a change of order, since in the virtual desktop X stacks a
newly shown window of another program above it whatever Wine's order says --
and when the foreground window fills its monitor the bar goes behind it and
that window is raised above it in X.

Gate: make test-topbar; test-taskbar and test-taskbarlooks expect the bar
topmost.
